--- body ---
## Context
The author asked on 2026-10-21 who defined the 15-file limit, why, and whether its cost is worth it, then
asked Fable (option b) and said go. Origin: `rules/workflow.md` "Monster ticket" (2026-07-11, the author):
15+ files is a signal to decompose, "a signal, not a wall", with a waiver. On 2026-09-23 gaze made it a hard
stop (`fix(gaze): refuse unreviewable PR size before review`): 15 or more content-bearing files returns
ESCALATE before any review unless a waiver says the change is indivisible; raid has a pre-flight count too.

Evidence for: `memory/journal/2026/2026-10-04-zotero-train-breaker-and-the-review-it-cost.md` (a full panel on
a parked big PR found a real introduced blocker). Evidence against: the same journal (the stop fired on
rename arithmetic and the PR got zero independent review), and 2026-10-21: the review-pr fold became three
stacked PRs, the gate activation two, the wording-pin cut two PRs and ticket 1182 two more; each merge into
`main` now needs its own gate record (about 90 s), stacked PRs retarget after each merge, and review seats
flagged half-consistent states between the pieces.

Decision (author's, with Fable's advice): option (b). Keep the signal; delete the hard stops, the waiver and
their tests; replace the count by a coverage rule on the output side. Not counting changed lines (it would
misfire on generated files, fixtures and moved paragraphs as files did on renames); not deleting the
workflow.md sentence.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Delete, in one commit so a single revert restores everything: `skills/gaze/references/setup-and-breaker.md`
      (the `pr_files` computation, the 15-file stop, § Waiver; keep what collection and the anchor check
      still need, folded into the gaze skill or a smaller reference), `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` (`--waive-breaker`
      in the argument hint and body, the `circuit_breaker: un-reviewable | waived` result field, the
      file-count bullet of § Circuit breakers; keep `multi_ticket` and the missing-ticket breaker),
      `skills/raid/SKILL.md` (the pre-flight count and split warning, the NEEDS-AUTHOR-via-waiver text;
      keep the breakers for a missing ticket and an exhausted re-gate), `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` (the
      NEEDS-AUTHOR-on-waiver rule and the `Review-scope: indivisible` line), the tests
      `tests/test_gaze_breaker_counting.py` and `tests/test_raid_breaker_gate.py`, and any script that exists
      only for the count (check `scripts/raid-breaker.py` is not also the loop breaker before removing it).
- [ ] `rules/workflow.md`: the waiver cross-reference becomes one sentence: a large diff splits the review,
      not necessarily the PR. The 15-file signal paragraph stays.
- [ ] The replacement, stated once in gaze: when a diff is large the orchestrator partitions it into review
      groups (by directory or concern, about 400 lines or fewer each), assigns seats per group, and the result
      lists the groups and which seat read which. A group no seat read makes the result FINDINGS (never
      REVIEWED), with the unread group named. No test pins this wording (no second-order guards).
- [ ] A grep for the deleted names (`waive-breaker`, `un-reviewable`, `Review-scope: indivisible`,
      `pr_files`, the two test names) across `skills/`, `scripts/`, `rules/`, `tests/` finds nothing live;
      `docs/` keeps history. Catalog regenerated; drift check clean.
- [ ] The regret trigger is recorded in the ticket log: a large PR merges after a REVIEWED whose seats read
      the surface and a blocker surfaces on `main` that a split would have caught; the signal is a `/roar`
      entry naming a post-merge blocker on a PR whose result lists a group over the cap or no seat for a group.
- [ ] Because the wall is still standing while this lands, split the PR if it needs more than 14 files, never
      a waiver; the deletion commit stays whole for rollback.
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime.
